#edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049626 #edb/ref 1031 "Subtracting a Negative Number" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049626 #edb/ref 1033 297 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049626 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "066efed6-041e-5946-85d0-c8b308da2022" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050012 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048345 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050012 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186092188 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050012 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186092192 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050012 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186092303 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050012 #edb/ref 1031 "Solving Problems Using the Four Operations on Rational Numbers" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050012 #edb/ref 1033 1024 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050012 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "2616710e-7f3d-5028-b0fe-1ed436c185da" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050371 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049618 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050371 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186184241 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050371 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186184242 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050371 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186184243 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050371 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186184244 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050371 #edb/ref 1031 "Addition in Scientific Notation With Different Powers of Ten" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050371 #edb/ref 1033 3843 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050371 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "43f5b613-82d3-572b-9dfd-8aef80e05cd6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096463 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4760" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096463 #edb/ref 1071 "Luisa has an overdraft facility authorized by her bank. Her bank balance on Monday was $\\[math] 173.25$. On Tuesday, Luisa decided to withdraw $\\[/math] 250.70$ to buy a laptop. What is Luisa's bank balance at the end of the day on Tuesday?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096463 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0d40f932-5646-5b71-b427-0b9477784939" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096463 #edb/ref 1074 "To find Luisa's bank balance at the end of the day on Tuesday, we subtract the amount of money Luisa spent on the laptop from the starting balance, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\[math] 173.25 - \\[/math] 250.70 = -\\[math] 77.45\n$$\n\nTherefore, Luisa's bank balance at the end of the day on Tuesday was $-\\[/math] 77.45$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096464 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4761" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096464 #edb/ref 1071 "Nazareth is doing an experiment in her Chemistry class. She heated a liquid whose initial temperature was $-5.6^{\\circ} \\, \\textrm{C}$. After several minutes, the temperature of the liquid rose by $4.7^{\\circ} \\, \\textrm{C}$, at which point she decided to end the experiment. What was the final temperature of the liquid?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096464 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f6286c4b-0268-5430-88f4-f6185180f010" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096464 #edb/ref 1074 "To determine the final temperature of the liquid, we add the change in temperature to the initial temperature of the liquid. This gives\n\n$$\n-5.6^{\\circ}\\,\\textrm{C} + 4.7^{\\circ}\\,\\textrm{C} = -0.9^{\\circ}\\,\\textrm{C}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the temperature of the liquid at the end of the experiment was $-0.9^{\\circ}\\,\\textrm{C}$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096465 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4763" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096465 #edb/ref 1071 "The city of Kaspiysk, in Russia, is $52.5$ feet below sea level, while the city of La Plata, in Argentina, is $83.2$ feet above sea level. What is the difference between the elevations of both cities?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096465 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "856921bd-1130-5b5f-8979-55ff188ac9ff" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096465 #edb/ref 1074 "To calculate the difference between the elevations of both cities, we must calculate the difference between the city with the highest elevation and the city with the lowest elevation. That is, we must calculate $83.2 - (-52.5)$. This gives\n\n$$\n83.2 - (-52.5) = 83.2 + 52.5 = 135.7 \\, \\textrm{ft}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096466 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4764" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096466 #edb/ref 1071 "In Chicago, the average temperature in December is $-1.5^{\\circ} \\, \\textrm{C}$. Then in January, the average temperature decreases by $3.5^{\\circ} \\, \\textrm{C}$ compared to December. Finally, in February, the average temperature increases by $2.6^{\\circ} \\, \\textrm{C}$ compared to the previous month. What is Chicago's average temperature in February?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096466 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a596d16e-8e1b-5c20-8d82-b25e5b746955" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096466 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we must determine the temperature in Chicago during the month of January. Since we are told that the temperature *decreases* on average $3.5^{\\circ} \\, \\textrm{C}$ compared to December, we *subtract* the variation in temperature from the average temperature in December. This gives\n\n$$\n-1.5^{\\circ} \\, \\textrm{C} - 3.5^{\\circ} \\, \\textrm{C} = -5.0^{\\circ} \\, \\textrm{C}\n$$\n\nNow we must determine the temperature during the month of February. Since we are told that the temperature *increases* on average $2.6^{\\circ} \\, \\textrm{C}$ compared to January, we *add* the variation in temperature to the average temperature of January. This gives\n\n$$\n-5.0^{\\circ} \\, \\textrm{C} + 2.6^{\\circ} \\, \\textrm{C} = -2.4^{\\circ} \\, \\textrm{C}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the average temperature in Chicago in the month of February is $-2.4^{\\circ} \\, \\textrm{C}$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096676 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048588 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096676 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048911 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096676 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186097329 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096676 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186097330 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096676 #edb/ref 1039 "Subtracting a Positive Number From a Smaller Positive Number" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096676 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186096463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096676 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "67067a80-2143-5532-b6e2-bbbf59d862c6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096677 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048546 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096677 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186097331 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096677 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186097332 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096677 #edb/ref 1039 "Adding a Positive Number to a Negative Number" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096677 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186096464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096677 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "c37cc3b9-6255-5fb6-bb61-6cae10cd9531" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096678 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049626 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096678 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186097327 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096678 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186097328 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096678 #edb/ref 1039 "Subtracting a Negative Number" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096678 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186096465 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096678 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "1ff8566a-bc65-50a8-bd72-354631883152" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096679 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186097333 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096679 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186097334 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096679 #edb/ref 1039 "Combining Operations on Negative Numbers" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096679 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186096466 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096679 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "3c9e3ef7-2d6f-526e-9ceb-fb21040b639e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096903 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186097526 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096903 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186097527 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096903 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186097528 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096903 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186097529 #edb/